# PART 8: DATABASE, STORAGE AND SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

Security is mandatory.

Inspect and preserve the existing RLS architecture.

For every relevant table, determine:

- Who can SELECT.
- Who can INSERT.
- Who can UPDATE.
- Who can DELETE.
- Whether the policy is restricted by authenticated user ID.
- Whether administrators have the intended access.
- Whether landlords can access only their own records.
- Whether students can access only permitted public accommodation data.

For Storage, inspect:

- Bucket existence and visibility.
- MIME restrictions.
- File size limits.
- INSERT policies.
- SELECT policies.
- UPDATE policies.
- DELETE policies.
- Folder ownership enforcement.
- Access to private verification documents.
- Access to property images.

Do not assume that a private bucket is secure merely because it is marked private. Its policies must also be correct.

Never use the Supabase service-role key in frontend code.

Never trust frontend role checks as the only security boundary.

Never allow students or landlords to retrieve another user's private verification documents.

Never allow users to approve their own verification submissions.

Never allow an unverified landlord to perform operations reserved for verified landlords.

Use server-side validation and database enforcement for sensitive operations.

Do not weaken RLS simply to make a failed query return data.

